// Repro 15 — GITI-019: interpolation whose expression uses `||` (or `&&`)
// emits illegal JS because the compiler's auto `?? ""` wrap is not
// parenthesized around the logical operand.
//
// Source: `${ expr || "fallback" }` — a common "default text" idiom.
//
// The compiler wraps every text interpolation in `String( <expr> ?? "" )`
// to coerce null/undefined to empty string. When <expr> itself contains a
// top-level `||` (or `&&`), the emit becomes:
//
//   String(e.description || "(no message)" ?? "")
//
// which is a JS SyntaxError: the `??` operator may NOT be combined with
// `||` or `&&` without explicit parentheses (ES2020 short-circuit
// ambiguity rule). Node reports: "SyntaxError: missing ) after argument list".
//
// Correct emit must parenthesize the source expression before appending
// the coalesce guard:
//
//   String((e.description || "(no message)") ?? "")
//
// The defect is specific to the `for ... lift` loop emit path: there the
// per-item interpolation is built with `createTextNode(String(expr ?? ""))`.
// A direct top-level reactive interpolation instead takes the
// `el.textContent = expr` path (no `?? ""` wrap) and does NOT trip the bug —
// so the repro must use a lift loop to surface it.
//
// To reproduce:
//   bun run compiler/src/cli.js compile ui/repros/repro-15-interp-logical-or-coalesce-mix.scrml -o /tmp/r15
//   grep "createTextNode" /tmp/r15/repro-15-interp-logical-or-coalesce-mix.client.js
//     -> ...createTextNode(String(e.description || "(no message)" ?? ""))
//   node --check /tmp/r15/repro-15-interp-logical-or-coalesce-mix.client.js
//     -> SyntaxError: missing ) after argument list
//
// Runtime impact: any giti UI page using the `${ x || "default" }` idiom
// inside a `for ... lift` loop fails to parse its client bundle. Surfaced
// in 3 of 5 pages (status, history, diff) immediately after GITI-014's fix
// unblocked those bundles.

<program>

${
  @entries = [{ description: not }]
}

<ul>
  ${
    for (let e of @entries) {
      lift <li>${e.description || "(no message)"}</li>
    }
  }
</ul>

</program>
